  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In a resource's ACL, when an acl:agentClass is set to foaf:Agent or acl:AuthenticatedAgent, the Fedora implementation should grant access to all users (",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://github.com/solid/web-access-control-spec#public-access-all-agents)."
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://github.com/solid/web-access-control-spec#public-access-all-agents) ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "or all authenticated users, respectively.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Currently both foaf:Agent and acl:AuthenticatedAgent is ignored.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Test ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://fedora.info/2018/06/25/spec/#resource-authorization"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "5.0-D and 5.0-E",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " in the CTS should pass once this issue is resolved.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
