  "description": "<p>In a resource's ACL, when an acl:agentClass is set to foaf:Agent or acl:AuthenticatedAgent, the Fedora implementation should grant access to all users (<a href=\"https://github.com/solid/web-access-control-spec#public-access-all-agents).\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/solid/web-access-control-spec#public-access-all-agents) </a>or all authenticated users, respectively.</p>\n\n<p>Currently both foaf:Agent and acl:AuthenticatedAgent is ignored.</p>\n\n<p>Test <a href=\"https://fedora.info/2018/06/25/spec/#resource-authorization\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">5.0-D and 5.0-E</a> in the CTS should pass once this issue is resolved.</p>",
